<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Wells Fargo cut to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Wells Fargo cut to hold.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gerard Klauer Mattison said it downgraded Wells Fargo and Co to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- cited poor execution of merger with First Interstate as primary reason.</p>
<p>-- said adverse effects from merger difficulties include &quot;lost revenues from fleeing customers and likely disappointing earnings at least for the remainder of 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>-- also said that if Warren Buffett continues to reduce Berkshire Hathaway Inc's holdings in Wells Fargo, &quot;this could weigh heavily on the stock price.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Shares were up 7/8 to 258-1/8.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
